s, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n? Go map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and write, no newline. That changes body. Need keep same response bodies. Could use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) for success. But if user struct with fields Name, Email", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0030493689700961113], [760, -6.889895915985107]], [[1144, -9.536788638797589e-06], [14235, -12.245502471923828]], [[4087, -0.01384427584707737], [310, -4.504176139831543]], [[1156, -0.03368585556745529], [303, -3.639467477798462]], [[579, -0.216334730386734], [25, -2.371713161468506]], [[1622, -0.003834137925878167], [3296, -6.3499627113342285]], [[13, -0.33125150203704834], [25, -1.613121509552002]], [[14235, -0.03624610975384712], [1165, -4.02829647064209]], [[89109, -0.3421344459056854], [7936, -1.7537612915039062]], [[5805, -0.0002672433329280466], [2400, -8.637443542480469]], [[9830, -0.026625722646713257], [6795, -3.691493034362793]], [[6795, -2.9445127438521013e-05], [17369, -11.914002418518066]], [[1083, -1.4222469329833984], [47781, -1.5764751434326172]], [[1228, -0.09560569375753403], [2400, -2.802133321762085]], [[470, -3.2187024771701545e-05], [5568, -10.605868339538574]], [[5568, -0.0029786438681185246], [74243, -6.1234354972839355]], [[440, -0.8865321278572083], [25, -1.894569754600525]], [[2708, -0.035803377628326416], [1810